      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "As for figuring out what's becoming more sensitive/infuential as voltage goes up, ..... WHY is your `vref` pnp branch lacking the `XM4`/`XM3` equivalent?\nAlso beware that you're doing.... well, I mean, it's obviously substantially different, but why is yours \"better\"?: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brokaw_bandgap_reference\nAt least regarding that you have base collector shorted on your pnp's and the linked has all 3 terminals of each one of the two npn's it has at different voltages.",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
